    "q-7798": {
      "dom_id": "step-q7798",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8{y}^{′}+16y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\text{ }\\text{ }{y}^{′}(1)=-1.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+16{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =4$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4x}+Bx{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nLet us find constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=-1.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{4x}+4Bx{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B$:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{4}+B{e}^{4}=2 \\\\ 4A{e}^{4}+5B{e}^{4}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=11{e}^{-4},B=-9{e}^{-4}.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =11{e}^{-4}\\cdot {e}^{4x}-9{e}^{-4}\\cdot x{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =11{e}^{4x-4}-9x{e}^{4x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-7798-a",
